WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.440
Every plant food we eat is a part of a plant.

2
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.560
Roots, stems, leaves, flowers, and fruits each have a job.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.580
A carrot is a root, and lettuce is a leaf.

4
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.480
Sort the foods to find which part each one is.

5
00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:20.613
You need a big sheet of paper and markers, and foods from the grocery store.

6
00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:24.293
Get a carrot, lettuce, broccoli, an apple, and a tomato.

7
00:00:25.293 --> 00:00:27.353
Add a potato and celery as trick cards.

8
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:31.557
Draw a plant with roots, stem, leaves, flower, and fruit.

9
00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.977
An adult washes the food and cuts the apple and tomato in half.

10
00:00:36.857 --> 00:00:40.077
Your child places each food on the drawing, and guesses its part.

11
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.770
Look for clues. Seeds inside means fruit, so a tomato is a fruit.

12
00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.970
A potato is not a root.

13
00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:49.990
It is an underground stem.

14
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.923
Stay with your child while food is out.

15
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.043
An adult does all the cutting.

16
00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:58.243
Check for allergies before anyone tastes anything.
